#
# ABox fixture for the probability-layer competency question "probability model for a
# reasoning request + its logic: lowering + preservation". It carries a REAL A-box
# triple ?request logic:probabilityModel ?model, where ?model is a math: dependency
# model (a math:BayesianNetwork). The math:BayesianNetwork class declares its logic:
# lowering (math:probabilityModelLowering → logic:DependencyModel) and its preservation
# polarity (logic:preservationKind logic:ExactPreservation) in the merged ontology, so
# the seam is live end-to-end via the logic:probabilityModel predicate. Unioned onto
# the merged ontology by gmeow:cqDataFile.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# The reasoning request (a world) declares the probability model governing its inference.
ex:bnQuery a logic:World ;
    logic:probabilityModel ex:sprinklerNet .

# The declared model is a math: dependency model that lowers into logic:.
ex:sprinklerNet a math:BayesianNetwork ;
    math:dependencyGraph ex:sprinklerDag .
ex:sprinklerDag a math:MathematicalObject .
